        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9bf43be7-059d-5263-8ed0-ce25c793154a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Entabeni Game Reserve\n- Animals: South African cheetah, Transvaal lion, African bush elephant, South African giraffe, African leopard, warthog, African buffalo, hippopotamus\n- Concepts: IUCN conservation status, cheetah subspecies\n\nFacts:\n- Since 1986, the South African cheetah has been classified as Vulnerable by the IUCN.\n- The South African cheetah, also called the Namibian cheetah, is the nominate cheetah subspecies and the most numerous cheetah subspecies native to Southern Africa.\n- Entabeni Game Reserve is home to the South African cheetah.\n- Entabeni Game Reserve is home to Transvaal lion, African bush elephant, South African giraffe, African leopard, warthog, African buffalo, hippopotamus, and other safari animals in a variety of habitats.",
